1
00:00:01,000 --> 00:00:03,000
Hello and welcome!

2
00:00:03,000 --> 00:00:06,000
How about some piping hot fried chicken?

3
00:00:06,000 --> 00:00:09,000
If you don't mind, please tap your phone there.

4
00:00:11,000 --> 00:00:12,000
Here you are, sir!

5
00:00:12,000 --> 00:00:15,000
Go ahead and take your lottery ticket for the campaign we're running!

6
00:00:15,000 --> 00:00:17,000
Draw one, please!

7
00:00:19,000 --> 00:00:21,000
By any chance...

8
00:00:21,000 --> 00:00:25,000
Were you pestering me so hard yesterday just to get me to do this?

9
00:00:25,000 --> 00:00:28,000
Hey, why not? It's on your way home anyway, right?

10
00:00:28,000 --> 00:00:31,000
Besides, you buy your dinner at convenience stores every day!

11
00:00:31,000 --> 00:00:32,000
Yeah, that's true.

12
00:00:32,000 --> 00:00:36,000
I haven't seen you since the festival. How's Runa been doing?

13
00:00:36,000 --> 00:00:39,000
Yeah, she seems to be studying hard.

14
00:00:39,000 --> 00:00:41,000
Is that right?

15
00:00:41,000 --> 00:00:45,000
She calls me every once in a while, but we hardly ever get to see each other.

16
00:00:45,000 --> 00:00:48,000
Oh my, he a friend of yours, Akane?

17
00:00:48,000 --> 00:00:49,000
Miss Shinohara!

18
00:00:49,000 --> 00:00:51,000
He's quite a looker.

19
00:00:51,000 --> 00:00:54,000
Yeah, he really is. We met playing the same game.

20
00:00:54,000 --> 00:00:56,000
His face was so gorgeous!

21
00:00:56,000 --> 00:00:58,000
He could be an actor.

22
00:00:58,000 --> 00:01:00,000
My heart's pounding!

23
00:01:00,000 --> 00:01:01,000
Okay, I'll be heading.

24
00:01:01,000 --> 00:01:03,000
My shift will be over soon, so wait for me, okay?

25
00:01:03,000 --> 00:01:05,000
Let's go home together!

26
00:02:36,000 --> 00:02:39,640
Oh, look at him waiting so faithfully.

27
00:02:39,960 --> 00:02:41,840
Are you two dating as well?

28
00:02:41,960 --> 00:02:43,220
Oh, no, we're not.

29
00:02:43,480 --> 00:02:46,620
He seems to have a hard time dealing with women, so it's not like that.

30
00:02:46,840 --> 00:02:48,400
Well, that is a crying shame.

31
00:02:48,560 --> 00:02:51,020
But that doesn't stop you from liking him now, does it?

32
00:02:51,420 --> 00:02:53,980
You were so determined to keep him from leaving.

33
00:02:55,080 --> 00:02:57,980
Yeah, well, I don't know about that.

34
00:02:58,340 --> 00:03:00,780
Amazing! Spoken exactly like a true maiden.

35
00:03:00,780 --> 00:03:09,540
I guess it is true that, compared to when we first met each other, Yamada seems to be a lot more willing to open up to me.

36
00:03:10,740 --> 00:03:15,360
From the time we've spent together, I can see that he's actually a really sweet guy.

37
00:03:16,340 --> 00:03:17,420
Eh, good work today.

38
00:03:17,620 --> 00:03:19,340
The thought does cross my mind.

39
00:03:19,820 --> 00:03:20,540
Thanks for waiting!

40
00:03:22,040 --> 00:03:27,400
Even if we're only linked by a game, I still find happiness in the fact that we're able to get closer.

41
00:03:27,400 --> 00:03:34,420
But now that I think about it, the same goes for Eita and Runa too, doesn't it?

42
00:03:36,480 --> 00:03:39,200
You know, I didn't ask you to visit me for the lottery.

43
00:03:39,680 --> 00:03:44,780
Actually, I wanted to give you this bento box I made for you, as a way of saying thank you.

44
00:03:45,180 --> 00:03:45,780
For what?

45
00:03:46,180 --> 00:03:46,860
My computer.

46
00:03:47,540 --> 00:03:50,020
Since I couldn't really do much for you during the festival.

47
00:03:50,580 --> 00:03:52,440
It's really not that big of a deal.

48
00:03:52,440 --> 00:03:58,380
Now that my penny-pinching days are over for the time being, there's a pretty lavish feast in there.

49
00:04:01,180 --> 00:04:04,260
For some reason, I can't shake this feeling.

50
00:04:04,860 --> 00:04:07,540
Like, I shouldn't see him in a romantic light.

51
00:04:08,220 --> 00:04:09,360
But I'm not sure why.

52
00:04:09,360 --> 00:04:17,860
Uh-oh, I sneezed in front of someone who was about to take entrance exams.

53
00:04:18,100 --> 00:04:18,840
Are you sick?

54
00:04:19,340 --> 00:04:20,640
Uh, I'm not sure.

55
00:04:21,180 --> 00:04:22,660
Did I have a mask in here?

56
00:04:22,660 --> 00:04:35,980
You find one?

57
00:04:35,980 --> 00:04:37,700
Uh-huh.

58
00:04:52,660 --> 00:04:59,140
I hope that it doesn't get any worse.

59
00:04:59,800 --> 00:05:00,380
You're cold?

60
00:05:04,560 --> 00:05:05,280
Yeah.

61
00:05:06,800 --> 00:05:07,780
Thank you.

62
00:05:15,780 --> 00:05:18,780
A guy who's super kind without realizing it.

63
00:05:19,040 --> 00:05:20,620
Isn't that pretty terrifying?

64
00:05:22,660 --> 00:05:24,460
Keep going.

65
00:05:25,220 --> 00:05:28,120
You let your guard down for one second, and it's like...

66
00:05:28,120 --> 00:05:29,760
Wait, is he actually into me?

67
00:05:30,100 --> 00:05:33,340
But it's just a delusion, and that's not the guy's intention at all.

68
00:05:33,700 --> 00:05:35,880
He's just being kind like any decent person.

69
00:05:36,380 --> 00:05:37,680
It's a terrifying trap.

70
00:05:38,140 --> 00:05:40,360
Before you move on, there's one thing I want to confirm.

71
00:05:40,880 --> 00:05:43,360
How can you be so sure that it's not his intention?

72
00:05:43,720 --> 00:05:45,820
Also, can I try something a little flashy on you?

73
00:05:45,900 --> 00:05:47,080
The theme's night, Butterfly.

74
00:05:47,380 --> 00:05:47,620
Huh?

75
00:05:47,720 --> 00:05:48,300
Please don't.

76
00:05:48,300 --> 00:05:49,920
I'll get in trouble at work.

77
00:05:50,640 --> 00:05:52,480
You haven't said any names yet.

78
00:05:52,660 --> 00:05:54,480
But we're talking about Yamada here, right?

79
00:05:55,160 --> 00:05:55,520
Yep.

80
00:05:55,800 --> 00:05:58,440
But you were so thrilled that he said you were out of his league.

81
00:05:58,880 --> 00:06:01,180
Honestly, I don't even think he meant much by that.

82
00:06:01,440 --> 00:06:01,640
Hmm?

83
00:06:02,140 --> 00:06:04,360
That's one of the things that makes it so terrifying.

84
00:06:05,160 --> 00:06:05,560
Hmm.

85
00:06:05,560 --> 00:06:10,820
All I know is that if a hot younger guy ever said that to me, even if he wasn't thinking

86
00:06:10,820 --> 00:06:13,520
straight, I wouldn't waste any time making a move.

87
00:06:13,880 --> 00:06:16,540
I have no idea why you're hemming and hawing about this.

88
00:06:16,700 --> 00:06:18,200
I'm not hemming and hawing, Momo.

89
00:06:19,020 --> 00:06:20,000
Oh, really now?

90
00:06:20,060 --> 00:06:23,280
Because from where I'm sitting, it looks like the most hemming and hawing you've ever done.

91
00:06:23,280 --> 00:06:27,860
I see how you light up when you're talking about Yamada, and you clearly have fun trying

92
00:06:27,860 --> 00:06:28,680
to figure him out.

93
00:06:29,400 --> 00:06:33,440
But this whole time, I haven't heard you say a word about what you want to do, Akane.

94
00:06:34,820 --> 00:06:36,480
And you need to figure that out.

95
00:06:36,700 --> 00:06:39,300
Because until you do, I can't really speak on it.

96
00:06:39,780 --> 00:06:40,500
Hmm.

97
00:06:40,500 --> 00:06:43,320
You're absolutely right.

98
00:06:44,120 --> 00:06:45,040
Night Butterfly?

99
00:06:45,120 --> 00:06:45,760
That I decline.

100
00:06:47,520 --> 00:06:48,660
Oh, it's Runa.

101
00:06:49,220 --> 00:06:50,020
Oh, that girl?

102
00:06:50,280 --> 00:06:51,240
I remember.

103
00:06:51,500 --> 00:06:53,000
The goth lolly middle schooler.

104
00:06:53,180 --> 00:06:53,740
That's right.

105
00:06:54,400 --> 00:06:54,820
Hi.

106
00:06:55,020 --> 00:06:55,420
Akane!

107
00:06:55,680 --> 00:06:56,800
Can we meet up right now?

108
00:06:57,320 --> 00:06:59,060
The guild is facing a crisis!

109
00:06:59,920 --> 00:07:00,200
Huh?

110
00:07:08,780 --> 00:07:09,800
I'm here, Runa.

111
00:07:10,840 --> 00:07:11,900
Thanks for waiting!

112
00:07:13,620 --> 00:07:16,140
Are you sure it's okay for you to be out at this hour?

113
00:07:16,620 --> 00:07:18,280
It's gonna get dark pretty soon.

114
00:07:18,560 --> 00:07:20,500
I came by taxi, so I'm totally fine.

115
00:07:20,740 --> 00:07:22,200
I'm going home by taxi, too.

116
00:07:22,840 --> 00:07:24,400
Then I guess there's no worries.

117
00:07:24,920 --> 00:07:25,440
Hey, listen.

118
00:07:25,720 --> 00:07:27,160
This afternoon, I was with Yamada and-

119
00:07:27,160 --> 00:07:28,000
Never mind that!

120
00:07:28,080 --> 00:07:29,100
Did you read my text?

121
00:07:29,560 --> 00:07:30,380
Yeah, sure.

122
00:07:30,800 --> 00:07:31,400
I read it.

123
00:07:31,640 --> 00:07:33,200
The guild's gonna be getting a new member.

124
00:07:33,880 --> 00:07:35,040
A new guild member?

125
00:07:35,220 --> 00:07:37,300
And yet another woman that I've never met before?

126
00:07:37,300 --> 00:07:39,660
It's unbelievable.

127
00:07:40,040 --> 00:07:42,260
When we started this game, we agreed to keep it in the family.

128
00:07:42,460 --> 00:07:43,680
Oh, I do like you now, Akane.

129
00:07:43,880 --> 00:07:44,420
But at this rate-

130
00:07:44,420 --> 00:07:45,820
Sounds a bit clickish.

131
00:07:45,920 --> 00:07:47,900
...my exams, it'll be a totally different guild!

132
00:07:48,460 --> 00:07:51,120
And if that wasn't enough, the fact that it's a woman makes it even worse,

133
00:07:51,180 --> 00:07:53,080
because women always find reasons to hate me!

134
00:07:53,280 --> 00:07:55,300
Well, I'm sort of looking forward to it, you know?

135
00:07:55,660 --> 00:07:58,500
Personally, I hope it's a girl who's new to online games like me.

136
00:07:58,780 --> 00:07:59,240
Oh, hey!

137
00:07:59,360 --> 00:08:00,280
I brought some hot chocolate.

138
00:08:00,420 --> 00:08:00,860
You want some-?

139
00:08:00,860 --> 00:08:01,320
Smoke it!

140
00:08:01,320 --> 00:08:05,620
Anyway, I've drawn up a plan to drive the interloper out immediately.

141
00:08:06,080 --> 00:08:06,400
Hey!

142
00:08:07,560 --> 00:08:09,460
Players who are new have their own anxieties,

143
00:08:09,640 --> 00:08:11,760
so it's on us to give them a warm welcome, okay?

144
00:08:14,780 --> 00:08:15,760
And you know what?

145
00:08:16,020 --> 00:08:18,900
Once you get to really know her, you might even end up as friends.

146
00:08:19,280 --> 00:08:20,940
Kind of like what happened with us, Runa.

147
00:08:20,940 --> 00:08:32,360
Doesn't the thought of becoming friends with someone

148
00:08:32,360 --> 00:08:34,560
you normally wouldn't cross paths with sound cool?

149
00:08:35,200 --> 00:08:36,920
I mean, doesn't it excite you?

150
00:08:37,080 --> 00:08:39,120
L-l-not at all!

151
00:08:39,400 --> 00:08:42,260
I already know that you're going to get along with her right away, Akane!

152
00:08:42,620 --> 00:08:45,480
Then you're going to start hanging out with her all the time and not me!

153
00:08:45,820 --> 00:08:47,500
No, silly, that's not true.

154
00:08:47,660 --> 00:08:48,900
I haven't even said anything to me.

155
00:08:48,900 --> 00:08:50,180
It's definitely gonna happen!

156
00:08:50,180 --> 00:08:53,440
There's nothing stopping all three of us from being friends, is there?

157
00:08:53,440 --> 00:08:54,700
I don't like odd numbers!

158
00:08:54,900 --> 00:08:56,060
One of us will be left out!

159
00:08:56,480 --> 00:08:59,380
Uh, let's all get along together, okay?

160
00:09:00,480 --> 00:09:00,920
Okay?

161
00:09:07,680 --> 00:09:10,160
It's like I have a jealous girlfriend now.

162
00:09:11,140 --> 00:09:13,360
Yeah, well, I'm not surprised.

163
00:09:13,860 --> 00:09:15,720
I knew that you'd say something like that.

164
00:09:15,720 --> 00:09:19,220
And my brother's like,

165
00:09:19,640 --> 00:09:22,180
This new girl is one of Yamada's important friends.

166
00:09:22,600 --> 00:09:25,060
So you better be respectful and welcome her nicely.

167
00:09:26,020 --> 00:09:26,740
Yamada's friend?

168
00:09:26,920 --> 00:09:28,280
She's a girl in his class.

169
00:09:29,040 --> 00:09:30,340
According to what I overheard,

170
00:09:30,440 --> 00:09:32,360
FPS games are usually more her style.

171
00:09:32,940 --> 00:09:35,000
But she wants to take a break and play an MMO.

172
00:09:35,000 --> 00:09:37,680
From what I can tell, they're pretty close.

173
00:09:38,180 --> 00:09:40,100
But when I called him to ask about her...

174
00:09:40,100 --> 00:09:40,900
Tell me!

175
00:09:41,180 --> 00:09:41,880
She's normal.

176
00:09:42,720 --> 00:09:45,540
Yamada played it cool and wouldn't spill any of the beans.

177
00:09:46,200 --> 00:09:48,860
And he said that if I was mean to her like when you joined,

178
00:09:48,940 --> 00:09:50,680
he would get really mad at me.

179
00:09:50,680 --> 00:09:53,980
So it's a girl that he's friends with.

180
00:09:54,620 --> 00:09:56,140
Kind of unexpected, huh?

181
00:09:56,560 --> 00:09:58,480
For Yamada to bring a girl into the guild.

182
00:09:58,980 --> 00:09:59,140
Huh?

183
00:09:59,680 --> 00:10:00,940
Yeah, I guess so.

184
00:10:01,640 --> 00:10:01,820
Ugh!

185
00:10:02,180 --> 00:10:03,100
Never mind that!

186
00:10:03,160 --> 00:10:04,260
Runa has a great idea!

187
00:10:04,560 --> 00:10:05,300
Give me your phone!

188
00:10:05,980 --> 00:10:06,220
Hm?

189
00:10:08,900 --> 00:10:09,980
What are you doing?

190
00:10:10,260 --> 00:10:12,040
I'm saving Yamada's number for you.

191
00:10:12,420 --> 00:10:14,020
That way you can call him Akane!

192
00:10:14,020 --> 00:10:16,680
He was being cautious when I asked about her,

193
00:10:16,800 --> 00:10:18,980
but I bet he'd be willing to open up to you.

194
00:10:19,680 --> 00:10:21,300
If I just knew what she's like,

195
00:10:21,520 --> 00:10:22,740
then Runa could rest easy.

196
00:10:26,200 --> 00:10:29,040
And apparently they just started dating after that.

197
00:10:29,280 --> 00:10:29,900
For real?

198
00:10:30,180 --> 00:10:32,640
But didn't they claim that they weren't each other's type?

199
00:10:32,760 --> 00:10:34,200
Well, yeah, but still.

200
00:10:34,420 --> 00:10:35,380
You know how it is.

201
00:10:35,520 --> 00:10:37,680
Even if you think there's no way it could happen,

202
00:10:37,680 --> 00:10:40,680
two people can always end up together over something trivial.

203
00:10:44,020 --> 00:10:47,100
Is it really possible

204
00:10:47,100 --> 00:10:49,940
for people to fall in love over something trivial?

205
00:10:51,120 --> 00:10:52,500
Yo, Prez, how goes it?

206
00:10:53,000 --> 00:10:55,060
Good evening, Okamoto and Yamada.

207
00:10:55,760 --> 00:10:56,060
Hello.

208
00:10:56,360 --> 00:10:57,600
So anyway, Prez,

209
00:10:57,700 --> 00:10:59,640
it was pretty funny how you came walking in here

210
00:10:59,640 --> 00:11:00,480
muttering to yourself.

211
00:11:00,860 --> 00:11:03,400
But I was directing the question at you two.

212
00:11:03,960 --> 00:11:05,300
About lovers, huh?

213
00:11:05,840 --> 00:11:07,040
The thing is,

214
00:11:07,040 --> 00:11:10,080
I'm not so sure we're the right people to ask about that subject.

215
00:11:10,260 --> 00:11:11,020
Yeah, good point.

216
00:11:11,660 --> 00:11:12,800
By the way, Yamada,

217
00:11:12,800 --> 00:11:15,180
thank you for helping me get into your guild

218
00:11:15,180 --> 00:11:17,460
and talking to the guild master for me.

219
00:11:17,860 --> 00:11:18,260
Sure.

220
00:11:18,880 --> 00:11:19,880
What's this about?

221
00:11:20,020 --> 00:11:20,960
A game I play.

222
00:11:21,300 --> 00:11:22,460
Oh, Foss, huh?

223
00:11:22,740 --> 00:11:24,420
I just started playing it myself,

224
00:11:24,780 --> 00:11:27,640
and I heard that it's better to be in one of the stronger guilds.

225
00:11:27,920 --> 00:11:30,420
So I asked Yamada to let me be a member of his.

226
00:11:30,580 --> 00:11:32,660
Well, Prez, you are a secret gamer, ain't you?

227
00:11:32,880 --> 00:11:34,660
I wouldn't say that I'm hiding it or anything,

228
00:11:34,840 --> 00:11:37,820
but it's not like I can talk about it casually with the other girls.

229
00:11:38,240 --> 00:11:39,760
They just talk about boys.

230
00:11:40,180 --> 00:11:40,820
No way!

231
00:11:40,820 --> 00:11:42,740
Does that mean you talk about boys with them, too?

232
00:11:43,440 --> 00:11:44,200
Not really.

233
00:11:46,480 --> 00:11:47,200
I see.

234
00:11:47,320 --> 00:11:49,980
So you've sacrificed your precious youth to gaming, too, huh?

235
00:11:49,980 --> 00:12:00,680
Not answering?

236
00:12:01,360 --> 00:12:02,600
It's an unknown number,

237
00:12:03,360 --> 00:12:05,240
and class is about to start anyway.

238
00:12:06,360 --> 00:12:07,200
It stopped.

239
00:12:07,200 --> 00:12:10,640
You seem to get a lot of random calls like that,

240
00:12:10,700 --> 00:12:11,520
don't you, Yamada?

241
00:12:11,980 --> 00:12:13,100
And when you do pick up,

242
00:12:13,140 --> 00:12:15,420
it's usually some girl confessing her love to you.

243
00:12:15,920 --> 00:12:17,620
If you wanted to, you could get any...

244
00:12:17,620 --> 00:12:18,620
Leave Yamada alone.

245
00:12:20,100 --> 00:12:21,260
Romance isn't his thing.

246
00:12:21,660 --> 00:12:22,400
Isn't that right?

247
00:12:24,620 --> 00:12:26,520
Well, no, I guess not.

248
00:12:26,520 --> 00:12:34,240
I thought so.

249
00:12:37,360 --> 00:12:38,660
I'm so hungry!

250
00:12:39,280 --> 00:12:40,900
If I don't eat soon, I'll die.

251
00:12:41,100 --> 00:12:43,500
Didn't you just have a hamburger before class started?

252
00:12:43,760 --> 00:12:45,480
Man, I'd kill for another burger.

253
00:12:45,680 --> 00:12:46,060
Again?

254
00:12:46,560 --> 00:12:48,640
Man, I want some fries to go with it, too.

255
00:12:48,640 --> 00:12:53,360
Hey, are you listening?

256
00:12:53,600 --> 00:12:54,100
One sec.

257
00:12:54,400 --> 00:12:56,280
Ooh, calling that person from earlier?

258
00:12:57,000 --> 00:12:58,640
If it's a girl with a sweet voice,

259
00:12:58,740 --> 00:13:00,060
pass the phone over to me, okay?

260
00:13:01,780 --> 00:13:02,900
Don't ignore me.

261
00:13:07,640 --> 00:13:08,080
Coming!

262
00:13:11,940 --> 00:13:12,380
Yes?

263
00:13:12,980 --> 00:13:13,740
I'm sorry.

264
00:13:14,100 --> 00:13:14,940
You just called me.

265
00:13:14,940 --> 00:13:14,960
Yamada?

266
